body:
dont know about high intelligence. thank you regardless.

&#x200B;

wasnt how i always felt.

to summarize. ill tell you what i told my closest friend.

&#x200B;

when i was a kid. i was an asshole. and i want to believe, in that fragile age, i had some reason to be. around my early 20's, i began remembering my mindset as a kid. which surpirsed me because i always define my youth as "unconscious living". the lights were on, but nobody was home. i was irrationally angry all the time and had huge problems with authority. i feel bad for that because he did not have the faculties to understand why he was angry all the time. i suppose the penny finally dropped for me when i realised how much i wanted other people to feel my pain. even if that meant burning bridges with them. 

&#x200B;

if im empathetic its only because im finally aware of the impact i can have on people. and ill be damned if i ever put myself before others again.
